      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From an economic perspective centered on housing needs, prioritizing supply increases through zoning reform aligns with solving the affordability crisis. Critics argue that while NIMBYism is a factor, it often masks genuine concerns about infrastructure strain, like overburdened schools or roads. Ultimately, the debate balances the macro goal of widespread housing affordability against the micro concerns of existing residents over preservation and quality of life.",
      "source": "target",
